# Temporal Verification Tripwire

Use this rule when a claim depends on current or recently changed facts:
- product or model versions
- APIs, SDKs, dependencies, release dates
- laws, policies, immigration guidance, institutional requirements
- market, company, or funding information
- calendar dates, time zones, deadlines

Invoke `hoveath-temporal-verification`.

Do not reject a user-provided version, path, policy, or date only because it looks newer than model memory. Verify first.

When verification is incomplete, mark the claim as unverified and state what source would close the gap.
